    "text": "Current Partners\nFederal Partners\nU.S. Department of Defense, Defense Health Agency\nU.S. Department of Health and Human Services, Administration for Community Living\nU.S. Department of Health and Human Services, Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services\nU.S. Department of Labor, Federal Employees’ Compensation\nU.S. Department of Veterans Affairs, Veterans Health Administration\nU.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement, Health Service Corps\nLaw Enforcement\nU.S. Department of Defense Office of Inspector General, Defense Criminal Investigative Service\nU.S. Department of Health and Human Services, Office of Inspector General\nU.S. Department of Justice, Criminal Division\nU.S. Department of Justice, Federal Bureau of Investigation\nU.S. Department of Justice, Office of the Inspector General, Fraud Detection Office\nU.S. Department of Labor, Employee Benefits Security Administration\nU.S. Department of Labor, Office of Inspector General\nU.S. Department of Veterans Affairs, Office of Inspector General\nU.S. Food and Drug Administration, Office of Criminal Investigations\nU.S. Office of Personnel Management, Office of the Inspector General\nU.S. Postal Service, Office of Inspector General\nAlabama: Office of the Attorney General, Medicaid Fraud Control Unit\nAlabama: Department of Insurance, Criminal Investigations Division\nAlaska: Department of Law, Medicaid Fraud Control Unit - Law Enforcement\nAmtrak: Office of the Inspector General\nArizona: Department of Insurance and Financial Institutions\nArkansas: Office of Attorney General, Medicaid Fraud Control Unit\nCalifornia: Department of Insurance, Fraud Division\nCalifornia: Department of Justice, Office of the Attorney General, Division of Medi-Cal Fraud and Elder Abuse\nColorado: Medicaid Fraud Control Unit\nConnecticut: Office of Attorney General, Medicaid Fraud Control Unit\nDelaware: Department of Insurance, Fraud Prevention Bureau\nDelaware: Department of Justice, Medicaid Fraud Control Unit\n