  {
    "title": "Medicare Provider Compliance Tips | CMS",
    "url": "https://www.cms.gov/training-education/medicare-learning-networkr-mln/compliance/medicare-provider-compliance-tips",
    "source_type": "webpage",
    "text": "Medicare Provider Compliance Tips\nThis educational tool offers Medicare provider compliance tips to help you order and bill items and services for your eligible Medicare patients and meet medical necessity requirements. Patient refers to a Medicare beneficiary, and we refers to CMS. The tool includes information about:\nAffected providers\nHCPCS and CPT codes\nBilling denials and preventing them\nDMEPOS general documentation requirements\nLab test order requirements\nRefill requirements\nResources\nFor updates or changes to Medicare Administrative Contractor (MAC) articles, local coverage determinations (LCDs), and national coverage determinations (NCDs), visit the Medicare Coverage Database (MCD) or find your MAC’s website . Learn more about articles, LCDs, and NCDs at MCD Help & Resources .\nPatients can visit Medicare.gov or call 1-800-MEDICARE (1-800-633-4227) for specific questions about their billing, claims, medical records, or expenses.\nNOTE:\nUse your browser’s zoom function to resize page content.\nAnticancer Drugs\nImmunosuppressive Drugs\nBreast Prostheses\nCardiac Pacemakers\nCommodes\nCPAP Devices\nGlucose Monitoring Supplies\nHospital Beds\nInfusion Pumps\nLenses\nLower Limb Orthoses\nLower Limb Prostheses\nManual Wheelchairs\nNebulizers\nNegative Pressure Wound Therapy\nOrthopedic Footwear\nOstomy Supplies\nOxygen\nPatient Lifts\nPneumatic Compression Devices\nRespiratory Assist Devices\nSpeech Generating Devices\nSpinal Orthoses\nSuction Pumps\nSurgical Dressings\nTherapeutic Footwear\nTracheostomy Supplies\nUrological Supplies\nVentilators\nWalkers\nWheelchair Options\nWheelchair Seating\nAmbulatory Surgical Centers\nCORF Services\nESRD Clinic Services\nHip & Knee Replacements\nHome Health Services\nHospice Services\nInpatient Rehabilitation Services\nSNF Services\nAmbulance Services\nAnnual Wellness Visits\nBacterial Cultures\nBlood Counts\nCataract Services\nChiropractic Services\nEchography & Sonography\nEnteral Nutrition\nEvaluation & Management\nIntravenous Immune Globulin\nOther Lab Tests\nParenteral Nutrition\nPhysical Therapy\nPodiatry\nPsychiatric Care\nUrinalysis\nVenipuncture\nDisclaimers\nCPT codes, descriptions, and other data only are copyright 2024 American Medical Association. All Rights Reserved.\nFee schedules, relative value units, conversion factors and/or related components are not assigned by the AMA, are not part of CPT, and the AMA is not recommending their use. The AMA does not directly or indirectly practice medicine or dispense medical services. The AMA assumes no liability for data contained or not contained herein.\nCPT is a registered trademark of the American Medical Association.\nView the Medicare Learning Network® Content Disclaimer and Department of Health & Human Services Disclosure .\nThe Medicare Learning Network®, MLN Connects®, and MLN Matters® are registered trademarks of the U.S. Department of Health & Human Services (HHS)."
