    "text": "Page 1\nMEDICARE QUARTERLY PROVIDER \nCOMPLIANCE NEWSLETTER \n\nARCHIVE \n\nThis page contains an archive of Medicare Quarterly Provider Compliance newsletters. Learn about how to address \ncommon billing errors and other claim review findings. We update this newsletter on a quarterly basis as new issues \nof the newsletter are released. \n\nAll newsletters are available to download, view, and print from the Medicare Learning Network® \n\nThe following resources allow you to search current and previous newsletters by common \nkeywords, phrases, and claim review findings. \n\n PROVIDER-SPECIFIC INDEX – a comprehensive index of all claim review findings from \ncurrent and previous newsletters. This index is customized and sorted by provider type to \nidentify those findings that impact specific providers. \n\n KEYWORD INDEX – a searchable index of common keywords and phrases from \nprevious newsletters.\n\nPage 2\nMedicare Quarterly Provider Compliance Newsletter \nJuly 2019 \n\nVOLUME & ISSUE DESCRIPTION DATE \nVolume 9, Issue 4 This issue addresses Comprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) and \nRecovery Audit findings that impact Physicians, Non-Physician \nPractitioners (NPPs), Doctors of Chiropractic and Durable Medical \nEquipment (DME) Suppliers. \nJuly \n2019 \nVolume 9, Issue 3 \n\n This issue addresses Comprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) and \nRecovery Audit findings that impact Durable Medical Equipment \n(DME) Suppliers, Physicians/Non-Physician Practitioners (NPPs), \nOutpatient Hospitals, Comprehensive Outpatient Rehabilitation \nFacilities, and Skilled Nursing Facilities. \n\nApril \n2019 \n Volume 9, Issue 2 \n\nThis issue addresses Comprehensive Error Rate Testing \n(CERT) and Recovery Audit findings that impact Physicians, \nDurable Medical Equipment Suppliers, Hospitals and Skilled \nNursing Facilities (SNFs). \nJanuary \n2019 \nVolume 9, Issue 1 This issue addresses Comprehensive Error Rate Testing \n(CERT) and Recovery Audit findings that impact Physicians, \nNon- Physician Practitioners (NPPs), Durable Medical \nEquipment Suppliers, other qualified individuals and Hospitals. \nOctober \n2018 \nVolume 8, Issue 4 This issue addresses Comprehensive Error Rate Testing \n(CERT) and Recovery Audit findings that impact Physicians, Non-\nPhysician Practitioners (NPPs), Durable Medical Equipment \nSuppliers, Outpatient Hospitals, Ambulatory Surgical Centers \n(ASCs) and Skilled Nursing Facilities (SNFs). \nJuly 2018 \n\nVolume 8, Issue 3 \nThis issue addresses Comprehensive Error Rate Testing \n(CERT) and Recovery Audit findings that impact Physicians, Non-\nPhysician Practitioners (NPPs), and Durable Medical Equipment \nSuppliers. \n\nApril 2018 \n\nVolume 8, Issue 2 \nThis issue addresses Comprehensive Error Rate Testing \n(CERT) and Recovery Audit findings on Advance Care Planning \nand an important Reminder on the Proper Use of Modifier 59 \nimpacting Physicians and Non Physician Practitioners (NPPs). \n\nJanuary \n2018 \n\nVolume 8, Issue 1 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nPhysicians, Non Physician Practitioners (NPPs) and Durable \nMedical Equipment (DME) Suppliers \nOctober \n2017 \n\nVolume 7, Issue 4 \nThis issue addresses common Comprehensive Error \nRate Testing (CERT) finding as well as an Office of \nthe Inspector General (OIG) report finding that \nimpacts non- physician practitioners, Skilled Nursing \nFacilities (SNFs), and hospitals. \n\nJuly 2017\n\nPage 3\nMedicare Quarterly Provider Compliance Newsletter \nJuly 2019 \n\nVOLUME & ISSUE DESCRIPTION DATE \n\nVolume 7, Issue 3 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nambulance suppliers, physicians, non- physician practitioners, \nclinical laboratories, End Stage Renal Disease (ESRD) facilities, \nand Skilled Nursing Facilities (SNFs). \n\nApril 2017 \n\n Volume 7, Issue 2 This issue addresses common Comprehensive Error Rate Testing \n(CERT) findings as well as an Office of the Inspector General \n(OIG) report finding that impacts hospitals and physicians \nJanuary 2017 \nVolume 7, Issue 1 This issue addresses common Comprehensive Error Rate Testing \n(CERT) findings as well as an Office of the Inspector General \n(OIG) report finding that impacts physician assistants, nurse \npractitioners, physicians, dentists, Durable Medical Equipment \nsuppliers, hospitals, clinical nurse specialist, and providers \nperforming hospital outpatient dental services \n October \n2016 \n\nVolume 6, Issue 4 \nThis issue addresses common Comprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) \nfindings as well as an Office of the Inspector General (OIG) report finding \nthat impacts physician assistants, nurse practitioners, physicians, dentists, \nDurable Medical Equipment suppliers, hospitals, clinical nurse specialist, \nand providers performing hospital outpatient dental services. \n\nJuly \n 2016 \n\nVolume 6, Issue 3 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nambulance suppliers, physicians, providers, Independent \nDiagnostic Testing Facilities (IDTFs), hospitals, ambulatory \nsurgical centers, outpatient providers, and Durable Medical \n\nApril \n2016 \n\nVolume 6, Issue \n2 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nphysicians, non- physician practitioners, Durable Medical \nEquipment suppliers, Inpatient Psychiatric Hospitals, and \noutpatient providers. \n\nJanuary \n2016 \n\nVolume 6, Issue \n1 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nhospitals, physicians and other providers submitting Part B \nprofessional claims, non- physician practitioners, Durable Medical \nEquipment suppliers, and clinical diagnostic laboratories. \n\nOctober \n2015 \n\nVolume 5, Issue \n4 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \ndurable medical equipment suppliers and non-physicians, \nphysicians, other qualified health professionals, outpatient \nfacilities and hospitals, and professional services. \n\nJuly 2015 \n\nVolume 5, Issue \n3 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nphysicians, other qualified health professionals, hospitals, radiation \ntherapy facilities, clinical laboratories, non- physician practitioners \nand home health agencies. \n\nApril 2015\n\nPage 4\nMedicare Quarterly Provider Compliance Newsletter \nJuly 2019 \n\nVOLUME & ISSUE DESCRIPTION DATE \n\nVolume 5, Issue \n2 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and Comprehensive \nError Rate Testing (CERT) findings as well as an Office of the \nInspector General (OIG) report finding that impact hospitals, \noutpatient hospitals, physicians, and durable medical equipment \n(DME) suppliers. \n\nJanuary \n2015 \n\nVolume 5, Issue \n1 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nhospitals, physicians, non- physician practitioners, and skilled \nnursing facilities. \n\nOctober \n2014 \n\nVolume 5, Issue \n1 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nhospitals, physicians, non- physician practitioners, and skilled \nnursing facilities. \n\nOctober \n2014 \n\nVolume 4, Issue 4 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nhospitals, physicians, and Durable Medical Equipment (DME) \nsuppliers. \n\nJuly 2014 \n\nVolume 4, Issue \n3 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nhospitals, physicians, and Durable Medical Equipment (DME) \nsuppliers. \n\nApril 2014 \n\nVolume 4, Issue 2 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nphysicians, suppliers, anesthesiologists, CRNAs, outpatient \nhospitals, and Part B professional services. \n\nJanuary \n2014 \n\nVolume 4, Issue 1 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \nphysicians, outpatient hospitals, inpatient hospitals, and ESRD \nfacilities. \n\nOctober \n2013 \n\nVolume 3, Issue 4 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that \nimpact home health providers, physicians, non-physician \npractitioners, durable medical equipment (DME) suppliers, \ninpatient hospitals, and outpatient hospitals. \n\nJuly 2013 \n\nVolume 3, Issue 3 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and Comprehensive \nError Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact physicians, \nchiropractors, non- physician practitioners, and inpatient hospitals. \n\nApril 2013\n\nPage 5\nMedicare Quarterly Provider Compliance Newsletter \nJuly 2019 \n\nVOLUME & ISSUE DESCRIPTION DATE \n\nVolume 3, Issue 1 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and Comprehensive \nError Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact inpatient hospitals, \nphysicians, and DME suppliers. \n\nOctober \n2012 \n\nVolume 2, Issue 4 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and Comprehensive \nError Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact inpatient hospitals, \nphysicians, and DMEPOS providers and suppliers. \n\nJuly 2012 \n\nVolume 2, Issue 3 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit and \nComprehensive Error Rate Testing (CERT) findings that impact \ninpatient hospitals and skilled nursing facilities. \n\nApril 2012 \nVolume 2, Issue 2 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit findings that \nimpact inpatient hospitals, ambulance providers, and \nDMEPOS suppliers. \n\nJanuary \n2012 \nVolume 2, Issue 1 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit findings \nthat impact physicians, DMEPOS suppliers, clinical social \nworkers, and inpatient hospitals. \n\nOctober \n2011 \nVolume 1, Issue 4 \n\nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit findings \nthat impact inpatient hospitals and DMEPOS suppliers. \n\nJuly 2011 \nVolume 1, Issue 3 This issue addresses common Recovery Audit findings that \nimpact inpatient rehabilitation facilities, physicians, non-\nphysician practitioners, radiology suppliers, inpatient hospitals, \nand outpatient hospitals. \n\nApril 2011 \nVolume 1, Issue 2 \nThis issue addresses common Recovery Audit findings that \nimpact inpatient hospitals, physicians, and Durable Medical \nEquipment (DME) suppliers. \n\nFebruary \n2011 \n\nVolume 1, Issue 1 \n\nIn this first issue, issues that impact a variety of provider types \nare presented to introduce the newsletter to a wide audience \nof providers. \n\nOctober \n2010"
