    "text": "Approved RAC Topics\nDo you have questions or concerns about the Recovery Audit Program? Please e-mail us at RAC@cms.hhs.gov . Please Do Not send Personal Health Information to this e-mail address.\nNote: CMS often receives referrals of potential improper payments from the MACs, UPICs, and Federal investigative agencies (e.g., OIG, DOJ). At CMS discretion, CMS may require the RAC to review claims, based on these referrals. These CMS-Required RAC reviews are conducted outside of the established ADR limits.\nIssue Name Sort descending\nReview Type\nProvider Type\nMAC Jurisdiction\nDate Approved\n0001 - Inpatient Hospital MS - DRG Coding Validation\nComplex\nInpatient Hospital\nAll A/B MACs\n2017-02-01\n0002 - Cataract Removal: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nAmbulatory Surgical Center (ASC); Outpatient Hospital\nCGS, First Coast, NGS, Noridian, Novitas, Palmetto, WPS (for DOS on/after 2/11/2024)\n2017-02-01\n0003 - Sacral Neurostimulation: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nAmbulatory Surgical Center (ASC); Inpatient Hospital; Outpatient Hospital; Professional Services\nAll A/B MACs (Urinary Frequency), CGS/Noridian and Palmetto (fecal incontinence)\n2017-02-01\n0008 - Bariatric Surgery-Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nInpatient Hospital; Outpatient Hospital\nAll A/B MACs\n2017-02-01\n0010 - Cardiac Positron Emission Tomography Scans: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nOutpatient Hospital; Professional Services\nJN, JL\n2017-02-01\n0011 - Inappropriate Billing of Home Visit Professional Service Evaluation and Management Codes During Hospital Inpatient Stay\nAutomated\nProfessional Services\nAll A/B MACs\n2017-02-01\n0012 - Blood Glucose Monitors with Integrated Voice Synthesizer: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nDME Physician/ DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-05-08\n0013 - Ankle-Foot Orthoses and Knee-Ankle-Foot Orthoses: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nDME Physician/DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-07-05\n0014 - Glucose Monitor Supplies Billed With Same Dates of Service as Glucose Monitor: Unbundling\nAutomated\nDME Physician/DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-02-01\n0016 - Continuous Passive Motion Billed without Total Knee Replacement or Total Knee Revision\nAutomated\nDME Physician/DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-02-01\n0018 - Spring-Powered Devices: Excessive Units\nAutomated\nDME Physician/ DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-02-01\n0019 - Durable Medical Equipment Billed while Inpatient: Unbundling\nAutomated\nDME Physician/DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-02-01\n0020 - Patient Lifts: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nDME Physician/DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-05-09\n0021 - Tracheostomy Suction Pumps and Suction Catheters: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nDME Physician/ DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-02-01\n0022 - Inpatient Psychiatric Admission Billed without Source of Admission Equal to \"D\"\nAutomated\nInpatient Hospital; Inpatient Psychiatric Facility (IPF)\nAll A/B MACs\n2017-02-01\n0023 - High Frequency Chest Wall Oscillation Devices: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nDME Physician/DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-02-01\n0024 - Spinal Orthoses: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nDME Physician/ DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-08-02\n0026 - Nebulized Drugs: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nDME Physician/ DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-04-11\n0028 - Annual Wellness Visit: Excessive Units\nAutomated\nProfessional Services\nAll A/B MACs\n2017-03-29\n0030 - Osteogenesis Stimulators: Medical Necessity and Documentation Requirements\nComplex\nDME Physician/DME Supplier\nAll DME MACs\n2017-02-01\n0037 - Hospital Services: Excessive Units\nAutomated\nProfessional Services\nAll A/B MACs\n2017-02-23\n0038 - Visits to Patients in Swing