tober 5). 65 Fed. Reg. 59434–59435. OIG Compliance Program for \nIndividual and Small Group Physician Practices. https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/\npkg/FR-2000-10-05/pdf/00-25500.pdf\n\nPage 4\n4Safeguarding Your Medical Identity CME Program\nFederal Trade Commission\n• Consumer Information. Identity Theft. https://www.consumer.ftc.gov/features/\nfeature-0014-identity-theft\n• Consumer Sentinel Network Data Book for January–December 2015. (2016, \nFebruary). https://www.ftc.gov/system/files/documents/reports/consumer-\nsentinel-network-data-book-january-december-2015/160229csn-2015 \ndatabook.pdf\nMedical and General Articles\n• Agrawal, S., & Budetti, P. (2012, February 1). Physician Medical Identity \nTheft. The Journal of the American Medical Association, 307(5): 459–460. \nhttp://jama.jamanetwork.com/issue.aspx?issueid=22488\n• American Medical Association. Electronic Funds Transfer (EFT) Toolkit. \nhttp://www.ama-assn.org/ama/pub/advocacy/topics/administrative-\nsimplification-initiatives/electronic-transactions-toolkit/eft-toolkit.page\n• Center on Budget and Policy Priorities. (2016, March 4). Policy Basics: Where \nDo Our Federal Tax Dollars Go? http://www.cbpp.org/cms/?fa=view&id=1258\n• Federal Trade Commission. Bureau of Consumer Protection. (2003, June). \nSecurity Check: Reducing Risks to Your Computer Systems. http://business.ftc.\ngov/documents/bus58-security-check-reducing-risks-your-computer-systems\n• Girion, L., & Helfand, D. (2010, August 27). U.S. Cracks Down on Healthcare \nFraud. Los Angeles Times. http://articles.latimes.com/2010/aug/27/business/la-\nfi-healthcare-fraud-20100827\n• Goodchild, J. Social Engineering: The Basics. CSO. (Updated December 2012). \nhttp://www.csoonline.com/article/514063/social-engineering-the-basics\n• Joszt, L. (2012, February 1). Risk of Physician Medical Identity Fraud. \nPhysician’s Money Digest. http://www.hcplive.com/physicians-money-digest/\nyour-money/Risk-of-Physician-Medical-Identity-Fraud\n• Kaiser Family Foundation. State Health Facts: Health Insurance Coverage of \nthe Total Population. (2015). http://kff.org/other/state-indicator/total-population/\n\nPage 5\n5Safeguarding Your Medical Identity CME Program\n• Keteyian, A. (2010, April 19). Digital Photocopiers Loaded With Secrets. \nCBS News. http://www.cbsnews.com/2100-18563_162-6412439.html\n• New York State Attorney General. (2012, February 16). As Rx Abuse Rises, \nA.G. Schneiderman Announces Prison Sentence for Woman Who Forged More \nThan 250 Painkiller Prescriptions. [Press release]. http://www.ag.ny.gov \npress-release/rx-abuse-rises-ag-schneiderman-announces-prison-sentence \nwoman-who-forged-more-250\n• Ponemon Institute. (2015, February). Fifth Annual Study on Medical Identity \nTheft. http://medidfraud.org/2014-fifth-annual-study-on-medical-identity-theft/\n• Medical Identity Fraud Alliance. http://medidfraud.org/\n• Sherman, T. (2011, September 13). Tuckerton Man’s Resolve Helps Uncover \nMultimillion-Dollar Health Care Fraud. The Star-Ledger. http://www.nj.com/\nnews/index.ssf/2011/09/tuckerton_mans_resolve_helps_u.html\n• V ogt, K. (2006, June 26). Safeguarding Identity: Tips to Stave Off a Growing \nProblem. American Medical News. http://www.amednews.com/article/20060626/\nbusiness/306269993/4/\nHealth Care Fraud in the News\n• Navigant. Table 3. Healthcare Fraud Settlements Reported in 2012 \n($250,000.+). http://www.navigant.com/~/media/WWW/Site/Page/Insights/\nFalse%20Claims%20Tracker/FCA_2013_quarterly_analysis_table_3.ashx\n• U.S. Department of Justice. Office of Public Affairs. (2010, August 26). \nAttorney General Holder and HHS Secretary Sebelius Host Second Regional \nHealth Care Fraud Prevention Summit in Los Angeles. https://www.justice.gov/\nopa/pr/2010/August/10-ag-965.html\n• U.S. Department of Justice. U.S. Attorney’s Office. Southern District of Florida. \n(2015, February 5). Broward County Resident Who Falsely Represented She \nWas a Licensed Medical Professional Was Sentenced to 17 Years Imprisonment \nfor Medicare Fraud. https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdfl/pr/broward-county-\nresident-who-falsely-represented-she-was-licensed-medical-professional\n• U.S. Department of Justice. U.S. Attorney’s Office. Middle District of Florida. \n(2012, January 5). Sarasota County Woman Sentenced for Health Care Fraud. \nhttps://www.fbi.gov/tampa/press-releases/2012/sarasota-county-woman-\nsentenced-for-health-care-fraud\n\nPage 6\n6Safeguarding Your Medical Identity CME Program\n• U.S. Department of Justice. Office of Public Affairs. (2014, December 17). \nMastermind of $56 Million Medicare Fraud Scheme and Doctor Plead Guilty. \nhttps://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/mastermind-56-million-medicare-fraud-scheme-\nand-doctor-plead-guilty \n• U.S. Department of Justice. U.S. Attorney’s Office. Eastern District of \nLouisiana. (2015, November 18). New Orleans Office Manager Sentenced for \nRole in $50 Million Fraud Scheme. https://www.justice.gov/usao-edla/pr/new-\norleans-office-manager-sentenced-role-50-million-fraud-scheme\n• U.S. Department of Justice. U.S. Attorney’s Office. Eastern District of \nCalifornia. (2012, January 12). Physician Sentenced to Eight Years in Federal \nPrison for Role in Massive Medicare Fraud Scam. https://www.fbi.gov/\nsacramento/press-releases/2012/physician-sentenced-to-eight-years-in-federal-\nprison-for-role-in-massive-medicare-fraud-scam \n• U.S. Department of Justice. Office of Public Affairs. (2012, February 7). Los \nAngeles Man Sentenced to 77 Months in Prison for Medicare Fraud Scheme \nResulting in More Than $18.9 Million in Fraudulent Claims to Medicare. \nhttps://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/2012/February/12-crm-174.html\n• U.S. Department of Justice. Office of Public Affairs. (2012, January 19). Patient \nRecruiter Pleads Guilty in Health Care Fraud Scheme. https://www.justice.gov/\nopa/pr/2012/January/12-crm-077.html\n• U.S. Department of Justice. Office of Public Affairs. (2012, January 9). Los \nAngeles Woman Sentenced to 60 Months in Prison for Her Role in a $6.2 \nMillion Medicare Fraud Scheme. https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/2012/\nJanuary/12-crm-038.html\nTo see the electronic version of this resource guide and the other products included in \nthe “Safeguarding Your Medical Identity” Toolkit, visit the Medicaid Program Integrity \nEducation page at https://www.cms.gov/Medicare-Medicaid-Coordination/ Fraud-\nPrevention/Medicaid-Integrity-Education/edmic-landing.html on the CMS website.\nFollow us on Twitter \n #MedicaidIntegrity\n\nPage 7\n7Safeguarding Your Medical Identity CME Program\nDisclaimer\nThis resource guide was current at the time it was published or uploaded onto the web. \nMedicaid and Medicare policies change frequently, so links to the source documents \nhave been provided within the document for your reference.\nThis resource guide was prepared as a service to the public and is not intended to \ngrant rights or impose obligations. This resource guide may contain references or links \nto statutes, regulations, or other policy materials. The information provided is only \nintended to be a general summary. Use of this material is voluntary. Inclusion of a link \ndoes not constitute CMS endorsement of the material. We encourage readers to review \nthe specific statutes, regulations, and other interpretive materials for a full and accurate \nstatement of their contents.\nApril 2016"
