    "title": "National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI) | CMS",
    "url": "https://www.cms.gov/national-correct-coding-initiative-ncci",
    "source_type": "webpage",
    "text": "NCCI Resources\nCMS updates the NCCI Policy Manual for Medicare once a year\nCMS revises the Medicare NCCI Correspondence Language Manual annually\nCMS updates the NCCI Policy Manual for Medicaid Services once a year\nAnnouncements\nMedicare: Effective Jan. 1, 2022, CMS implemented a new format for the Add-on Code (AOC) edit file. The format is a fixed-width text file. Review the new Medicare Add-On Code File Structure (PDF) .\nMedicare: The most recent edit files, including quarterly version update changes, are available on the PTP Coding Edits page , the Medically Unlikely Edits page , and the Add-On Code Edits page .\nThe National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI)\nThe Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI) promotes national correct coding methodologies and reduces improper coding, with the overall goal of reducing improper payments of Medicare Part B and Medicaid claims.\nThe Medicare National Correct Coding Initiative page provides information and edits related to the Medicare NCCI program.\nVisit the Medicaid National Correct Coding Initiative page for information and edits for the Medicaid NCCI program."
